From: Hanna Jose <hjose@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:12:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Description] : Adds packet-statistics handling in
 wanmgr_network_monitor.c for client lifecycle, including connect/disconnect
 tracking and per-client accounting flow.Creates/uses TRAFFIC_ACCT
 iptables/ip6tables chains, manages client state files, and logs RX/TX totals
 for IPv4/IPv6 and aggregated stats.

[RCA/Root Cause Analysis]:
WanManager previously lacked end-to-end orchestration to attach packet-accounting rules to active clients and collect stats at disconnect time.
Without unified rule programming and state tracking, per-client packet statistics were inconsistent, missing, or not properly cleaned up.

[Fix Description]:
Implements helper functions for client lookup, rule existence checks, rule add/delete, stats extraction, and disconnect-time reporting.
Gates behavior with packet-stats enable state and integrates rule/chain initialization so accounting is consistently applied across events.

Signed-off-by: Hanna Jose <hjose@qti.qualcomm.com>
